WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:06.760
Watching a movie at home just can't match
the experience of seeing it on the big screen.

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:12.400
Plenty of films are just fine to watch on
your home theater or portable device of choice,

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:17.720
but every year brings a new crowd of releases
that really need the big screen to be truly

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.520
appreciated.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:24.600
Here's a look at some of the biggest 2018
movies that demand to be seen in theaters.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.500
First Man

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:33.070
In First Man, Damien Chazelle 
is following up 2016's La La Land with a period

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.840
piece about the Apollo 11 moon landing.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:41.500
Starring Ryan Gosling as the legendary Neil
Armstrong, it looks to be a riveting drama

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:44.300
that will shine like a star on the big screen.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:51.260
Chazelle shot select scenes with IMAX 70 millimeter
film, and that's the way he intends for First

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:52.240
Man to be seen.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:58.059
The film revolves around the most famous lunar
mission of all time, and the Apollo 11 launch

00:00:58.059 --> 00:01:03.609
and subsequent landing on the moon is going
to look absolutely spectacular on a massive

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:04.100
screen.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:05.860
The Predator

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.920
Writer/director Shane Black is responsible
for some of the better action movies in recent

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:12.930
memory.

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:16.510
Considering this, The Predator is going to
be a must-see in theaters.

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:20.540
Few genres play as reliably well in theaters
as action and horror.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:26.020
A big screen brings out the true power of
explosive action, and an audience amplifies

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:28.850
the experience of seeing a horror movie.

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:34.040
The Predator looks to have everything we love
about going to the movies wrapped up in one

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.460
neat package.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:36.900
Creed II

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:43.920
2015 saw the Rocky franchise make an unlikely
comeback with Creed, which shifted the focus

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.780
from Rocky Balboa to the son of his old rival
Apollo Creed.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:54.100
The film nabbed a ton of critical acclaim,
all while telling an emotional, visually striking

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:54.600
story.

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:55.560
“Come on!

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.200
Don’t sit there!”

00:01:57.540 --> 00:02:02.240
“They’re trading shots in the kind of
back-and-forth action that most of us didn’t

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:02.820
expect to see.”

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:08.400
The journey of Adonis continues in Creed II,
and you don't want to miss it in theaters.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:14.480
Seeing a Rocky movie on the big screen with
an excited crowd is a special experience that

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.880
doesn't come around too often.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:17.940
Halloween

00:02:19.020 --> 00:02:24.840
Few cinematic boogeymen have delivered big-screen
scares quite as effectively over the years

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:29.240
as Michael Myers, and now he's back in a brand
new Halloween movie.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:34.080
Directed by David Gordon Green of Pineapple
Express fame and co-written by his frequent

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:39.590
collaborator Danny McBride, the film sees
original protagonist Laurie Strode come back

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.900
to take on the man who ruined her life.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.560
It looks to be a return to form for the series,
and with the greatest slasher villain of all

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.180
time returning to cinemas for the first time
in nearly a decade, you don't want to miss

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.800
the chance to see Halloween on the big screen.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:55.420
Venom

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:02.280
Spider-Man's goth symbiote twin makes his
solo big-screen debut in Venom, and this is

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.720
definitely one you need to see in a theater.

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:09.920
Director Ruben Fleischer has put together
a twisted, brutal, and witty take on the popular

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.430
Marvel anti-hero.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:16.599
Aside from the great cast led by Tom Hardy,
the effects look killer, and with an IMAX

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:20.630
release to accompany its standard theatrical
run, you aren't going to want to miss Venom

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.000
at a theater near you.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.280
"Eyes.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:24.440
Lungs.

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:25.480
Pancreas.

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.560
So many snacks, so little time."

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.840
Bohemian Rhapsody

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:39.040
Generations of Queen fans will never get to
see Freddie Mercury perform live, but Bohemian

00:03:39.049 --> 00:03:41.669
Rhapsody may be the next best thing.

00:03:41.669 --> 00:03:47.389
The bio-pic surveys the rise of Queen, including
multiple concert recreations, but the big

00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:50.520
draw here is the famous shows at Wembley Stadium.

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:56.140
Bohemian Rhapsody gives fans a chance to sit
in a theater and see a re-enactment of Queen's

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:59.740
biggest concerts of all time on a massive
screen.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:04.940
Tragically, that's about as close as anyone
can get to seeing Mercury tear up the stage

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:05.440
today.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:06.860
Aquaman

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:13.849
Jason Momoa's take on the King of Atlantis
is one of the strongest elements in the DCEU

00:04:13.849 --> 00:04:19.450
so far, and the full-length film starring
the aquatic hero looks absolutely amazing.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:24.610
Add in a killer cast that includes Patrick
Wilson, Nicole Kidman, and Amber Heard, and

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:27.380
Aquaman feels like it could be something special.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:32.260
All that said, the visual spectacle of Atlantis
itself could end up stealing the show.

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:37.380
The first trailer gives us a tantalizing glimpse
of the lush underwater kingdom, filled with

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:38.720
beautiful design and color.

00:04:39.009 --> 00:04:44.380
It remains to be seen whether Aquaman will
be an aquatic slam dunk, but a killer cast,

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:49.620
Atlantis, and more Momoa is enough to make
it a must-see at your local cineplex.

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:52.920
"I hear you can talk to fish."

